{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1773941108,"nonce":"O5JIe7wh3fgAZmr2J8k+MF9PxnI=","message":"**SDK per-message control flexibility**\n\nWith the SDK backend now live (Bug: 9bf8b4c), the model/hyperparam controls story is much stronger than originally scoped for PTY.\n\nEach user message triggers an independent `sdk.query()` call. `buildQueryOptions()` is called fresh per-prompt, meaning ALL of these can be changed between messages — not just at session start:\n\n- `model` — already wired to the sidebar selector\n- `systemPrompt` — can inject per-message context or override CLAUDE.md\n- `permissionMode`, `allowedTools` — granular tool gating per turn\n- `maxTurns`, `maxBudgetUsd` — per-query limits\n- `settingSources: [\"user\", \"project\", \"local\"]` — controls which CLAUDE.md files are read; re-read each query\n- `cwd` — can change the project context mid-conversation\n- `env` — environment variables passed to the SDK\n\nThis is a significant capability PTY does not have (PTY reads CLAUDE.md once at startup, model is fixed for the process lifetime). The SDK effectively gives us per-message granular control over the entire instruction context.\n\nImplications for this issue:\n- Model selector can switch models mid-conversation (already works)\n- A future \"system prompt injection\" field could modify instructions per-message\n- Thinking effort/budget could be per-message rather than per-session\n- CLAUDE.md hot-reload is free — each query re-reads settings sources","files":null}]}